DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccaaccooss(), ccaassiinn(), and ccaattaann() functions compute the principal value
     of the inverse cosine, sine, and tangent of the complex number _z, respec‐
     tively.  The ccaaccoosshh(), ccaassiinnhh(), and ccaattaannhh() functions compute the prin‐
     cipal value of the inverse hyperbolic cosine, sine, and tangent.  The
     ccaaccoossff(), ccaassiinnff(), ccaattaannff() ccaaccoosshhff(), ccaassiinnhhff(), and ccaattaannhhff() func‐
     tions perform the same operations in _f_l_o_a_t precision.  The ccaaccoossll(),
     ccaassiinnll(), ccaattaannll() ccaaccoosshhll(), ccaassiinnhhll(), and ccaattaannhhll() functions perform
     the same operations in _l_o_n_g _d_o_u_b_l_e precision.

     There is no universal convention for defining the principal values of
     these functions.  The following table gives the branch cuts, and the cor‐
     responding ranges for the return values, adopted by the C language.

     FFuunnccttiioonn    BBrraanncchh CCuutt((ss))            RRaannggee
     cacos       (-∞, -1) ∪ (1, ∞)        [0, π]
     casin       (-∞, -1) ∪ (1, ∞)        [-π/2, π/2]
     catan       (-∞*I, -I) ∪ (I, ∞*I)    [-π/2, π/2]
     cacosh      (-∞, 1)                  [-π*I, π*I]
     casinh      (-∞*I, -I) ∪ (I, ∞*I)    [-π/2*I, π/2*I]
     catanh      (-∞, -1) ∪ (1, ∞)        [-π/2*I, π/2*I]

